eft.  \\n- W4: across player discarded W4, so maybe safe? Unshown 3 left.  \\n- B5: across player discarded B5, unshown 3 left.  \\n- B4: unshown 4 left, no recent discards.  \\n\\nAlso consider my hand composition: I have many B tiles (B3,B4,B4,B5) and T tiles (T2,T3,T3). Maybe aim for half flush with bamboo? My melds: B6-7-8 chow (bamboo) and T7 pung (bamboo). So I have two bamboo melds already. If I can get more bamboo, I could go for half flush (only bamboo and honors). But I have no honors in hand. Alternatively, all chows?  \\n\\nBetter to discard isolated tile: W4 is isolated from other suits. T2 is isolated but near T3. B3,B4,B5 are connected. So worst tiles: W4 and T2. Among them, T2 might form chow with T3,T4 if I draw T4. W4 might form chow with W3,W5 but W3 is all gone (kong), so impossible. So W4 is dead for chow. Also W4 could be pair if I get another W4, but unshown 3 left.  \\n\\nDiscard W4 seems reasonable.  \\n\\nBut also consider scoring: I have pung of T7, which is simple, no fan. I need at least 8 fan to win. Currently potential patterns:  \\n- Half Flush (6 fan) if all tiles are bamboo and honors. My melds: B6-8 chow (bamboo), T7 pung (bamboo). My hand: T2,T3,T3 (bamboo), B3,B4,B4,B5 (bamboo), W4 (character). So if I discard W4, all hand tiles are bamboo. Then I have all bamboo + maybe honors? No honors. So full flush? Full flush is 24 fan: all tiles same suit. But I have T7 pung (bamboo) and B6-8 chow (bamboo) and hand all bamboo. That would be full flush! Wait: full flush requires all tiles of the same suit. My melds: B6,B7,B8 are bamboo (B is dots, not bamboo). Oh! Important: B is Dots (\\u997c), T is Bamboo (\\u6761). So my chow is B6,B7,B8 (dots), my pung is T7 (bamboo). They are different suits. So not same suit. So full flush not possible.  \\n\\nHalf flush: only one suit and honors. If I keep bamboo (T tiles) and discard dots and characters, I could aim for half flush. Currently I have one bamboo meld (T7 pung) and hand has T2,T3,T3 (bamboo). Also have dots: B3,B4,B4,B5 and chow B6-8 (dots). So to get half flush, I need to convert all dots to bamboo or honors, which is hard.  \\n\\nMaybe simpler: aim for all chows (2 fan) plus other patterns.  \\n\\nGiven the complexity, I should discard the most useless tile: W4 is character, no connection, and W3 is gone so no chow possibility.  \\n\\nAlso check if discarding W4 is safe: across player discarded W4, so maybe they don't need it. Unshown 3 left, but others might have pair.  \\n\\nAlternatively, T2: next player discarded T2, so maybe safe.  \\n\\nBut T2 can combine with T3 for potential chow if I get T1 or T4.  \\n\\nSo W4 is worse.  \\n\\nAlso B3,B4,B5 are connected, so keep them. B4 duplicates can be pair. T3 pair possible.  \\n\\nSo discard W4.  \\n\\nReason: W4 is isolated, with no chance to form chow since W3 is exhausted (kong by across player), and it's a different suit from my potential bamboo focus. Discarding it maintains flexibility with bamboo and dots sequences, and it appears relatively safe based on discard history.  \\n\\nAnswer: Play W4\"}"}
