hich is both seat and prevailing wind, so valuable for points. If I keep it and pair it, I get 4 points (Seat Wind 2 + Prevalent Wind 2). That's significant towards 8. So probably keep F1.  \n\nMy hand needs a pair and a meld. The easiest meld to form is a Chow using B3 and B4 if I draw B2 or B5. Or using W1 and W4 if I draw W2 or W3 or W5? W2 and W3 are low availability: W2:2 left, W3:0 left, W5:1 left. So not good. Alternatively, pair one of them and form a Chow with the other two? Unlikely.  \n\nSo best to keep B3 and B4 together for Chow potential, and keep F1 for point potential. Then discard either W1 or W4. Which is safer? W1 is terminal, might be more dangerous for giving others points, but many have been played. W4 is safer. But also, if I discard W1, I move towards All Simples (no terminals/honors) but I still have F1 honor, so not All Simples. To get All Simples, I need to discard F1 too. So maybe not aiming for All Simples.  \n\nConsidering opponents: next player has no melds, across has T1 pung and W3 kong, previous has no melds. Their histories show many discards. I should avoid discarding tiles that might complete their hands.  \n\nAcross has T1 pung and W3 kong, so they might be collecting winds or terminals? Not sure.  \n\nI think keeping F1 is good for points, and keeping B3,B4 for Chow potential. So discard W1 or W4. Between them, W1 is terminal, so if I discard it, I lose chance for Pung of Terminals or Honors (1 point) but I only have one. Better to discard W1 because it's less useful for Chow since W2 and W3 are scarce. W4 could pair with drawn W4, or form Chow with W3-W4-W5 (W3 gone, W5:1 left). So W4 has some potential.  \n\nBut W1 is more dangerous to hold if someone needs it for Thirteen Orphans or something, but unlikely.  \n\nI'll discard W1.  \n\nReason: I need to develop my hand towards a winning shape. Keeping B3 and B4 offers the best chance to complete a Chow in Dots suit, which fits with my existing Dots chows. Keeping F1 provides valuable wind points if paired. W1 is isolated and terminal with low chance to form a meld given the scarcity of W2 and W3. Discarding W1 is relatively safe given several have been played.  \n\nAnswer: Play W1"}
